  checkpoint {
    session_summary: "This summary captures the current state of the project, the architectural decisions made, and the pending actions for the next agent.\n\n### 1. Outstanding User Requests\n*   **Review and Approval:** The user requested a plan and visual representation of the \"Obsidian MCP Hybrid Retrieval Cockpit.\" I have implemented the UI components as a functional interactive mockup. The user needs to review these components and provide the \"go\" to proceed with full integration.\n*   **Status:** IMPLEMENTATION (Waiting for user approval).\n\n### 2. User Knowledge\n*   **Design Philosophy:** Strict adherence to the provided `vorlage.jpg` (Obsidian Vault Cockpit aesthetic). The user demands a \"hoch professionelles Design\" (high-end, elegant, futuristic).\n*   **Functional Requirements:**\n    *   Convert the provided text into an actionable, structured task list.\n    *   Include meaningful animations (e.g., frequency visualizers).\n    *   The design must be \"the only true template\" for this project.\n*   **Correction/Context:** Image generation tools were unavailable due to usage limits; therefore, I built the high-fidelity UI components directly as the \"screenshots\" and interactive mockups requested.\n\n### 3. Work Accomplished\n*   **Task Data Structure:** Created `src/data/tasksData.ts` containing the full 32-chapter implementation plan for the Obsidian MCP Hybrid Retrieval system.\n*   **UI Component Library:** Built four core components that replicate the requested \"Cockpit\" aesthetic:\n    *   `MountainSunsetBanner`: A dynamic, animated banner with a sunset mountain landscape and a real-time frequency visualizer.\n    *   `CircularGauges`: HUD-style telemetry cards displaying task progress, system specs, and retrieval metrics.\n    *   `TaskChecklistView`: An interactive, filterable task list with code snippet support and batch-processing capabilities.\n    *   `ArchitectureSimulator`: An interactive RRF (Reciprocal Rank Fusion) calculator and 3-layer architecture explorer.\n*   **Styling System:** Configured `src/index.css` with custom glassmorphic HUD utilities, glowing borders, and specific typography (Syne, JetBrains Mono, Plus Jakarta Sans) to match the requested aesthetic.\n\n### 4. Model Knowledge\n*   **Architecture:** The application is built using React 19 and Tailwind CSS 4. The UI is designed as a \"Cockpit\" dashboard with glassmorphic cards (`hud-card`) and glowing accents (`glow-orange`, `glow-cyan`).\n*   **Design System:**\n    *   **Typography:** `Syne` (Display), `JetBrains Mono` (Data/Telemetry), `Plus Jakarta Sans` (Body).\n    *   **Color Palette:** Deep obsidian/slate-purple (`#0b0914`) with orange/amber accents (`#ff7b39`) and cyan telemetry (`#22d3ee`).\n*   **Failures:** `generate_image` tool calls failed due to resource exhaustion. The UI components were built as the primary visual representation instead.\n*   **Constraints:** Adhered strictly to the `frontend-design` skill (no slop, tabular numerals, 60-30-10 color distribution).\n\n### 5. Files and Code\n*   **Edited/Created Files:**\n    *   `/metadata.json`: Updated with app title and description.\n    *   `/index.html`: Added Google Fonts and base body styling.\n    *   `/src/index.css`: Added custom HUD glassmorphism, glow utilities, and scrollbar styling.\n    *   `/src/data/tasksData.ts`: Created the 32-chapter task repository.\n    *   `/src/components/MountainSunsetBanner.tsx`: Created the animated banner component.\n    *   `/src/components/CircularGauges.tsx`: Created the telemetry HUD component.\n    *   `/src/components/TaskChecklistView.tsx`: Created the interactive task list component.\n    *   `/src/components/ArchitectureSimulator.tsx`: Created the RRF/Architecture simulator.\n*   **Viewed Files:**\n    *   `/skills/system_skills/frontend_design/SKILL.md`: Used to enforce design constraints (no slop, contrast, typography).\n\n### 6. Current Work and Next Steps\n*   **Immediate Next Step:** The next agent should wait for the user to review the components. Once the user gives the \"go,\" the next step is to integrate these components into `src/App.tsx` to create the main dashboard layout.\n*   **Relevant Skills:** The next agent must re-read `/skills/system_skills/frontend_design/SKILL.md` to ensure any further modifications remain compliant with the design constitution.\n*   **User Quote:** \"Mach den Plan damit ich schauen kann und dir das go geben kann\" (Make the plan so I can look at it and give you the go)."
    included_step_index_end: 35
    conversation_log_uris: "file:///.aistudio/artifacts/brain/701ae614-bcb5-4c42-8b5b-26b99136c74a/.system_generated/logs/transcript.jsonl"
    user_requests: "Here is the full initial file tree for the application:\n/.env.example\n/.gitignore\n/index.html\n/metadata.json\n/package.json\n/public/assets/aistudio/.gitignore\n/src/App.tsx\n/src/index.css\n/src/main.tsx\n/tsconfig.json\n/vite.config.ts\n\nThe following dependencies are installed:\n@google/genai: ^2.4.0\n@tailwindcss/vite: ^4.3.3\n@vitejs/plugin-react: ^6.1.1\ndotenv: ^17.2.3\nexpress: ^4.21.2\nlucide-react: ^0.546.0\nmotion: ^12.23.24\nreact: ^19.0.1\nreact-dom: ^19.0.1\nvite: ^8.3.0\n\nThe following devDependencies are installed:\n@types/express: ^4.17.21\n@types/node: ^22.14.0\n@types/react: ^19.3.0\n@types/react-dom: ^19.3.0\nautoprefixer: ^10.4.21\nesbuild: ^0.25.0\ntailwindcss: ^4.3.3\ntsx: ^4.21.0\ntypescript: ^7.0.2\n\nKey file contents:\n\n--- /.env.example ---\n```\n# GEMINI_API_KEY: Required for Gemini AI API calls.\n# AI Studio automatically injects this at runtime from user secrets.\n# Users configure this via the Secrets panel in the AI Studio UI.\nGEMINI_API_KEY=\"MY_GEMINI_API_KEY\"\n\n# APP_URL: The URL where this applet is hosted.\n# AI Studio automatically injects this at runtime with the Cloud Run service URL.\n# Used for self-referential links, OAuth callbacks, and API endpoints.\nAPP_URL=\"MY_APP_URL\"\n\n```\n\n--- /index.html ---\n```html\n<!doctype html>\n<html lang=\"en\">\n  <head>\n    <meta charset=\"UTF-8\" />\n    <meta name=\"viewport\" content=\"width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0\" />\n    <title>My Google AI Studio App</title>\n    <meta name=\"description\" content=\"An application built with Google AI Studio.\" />\n    <meta property=\"og:title\" content=\"My Google AI Studio App\" />\n    <meta property=\"og:description\" content=\"An application built with Google AI Studio.\" />\n    <meta property=\"og:type\" content=\"website\" />\n    <meta name=\"twitter:card\" content=\"summary_large_image\" />\n  </head>\n  <body>\n    <div id=\"root\"></div>\n    <script type=\"module\" src=\"/src/main.tsx\"></script>\n  </body>\n</html>\n\n\n```\n\n--- /metadata.json ---\n```json\n{\n  \"name\": \"\",\n  \"description\": \"\",\n  \"requestFramePermissions\": [],\n  \"majorCapabilities\": [\"MAJOR_CAPABILITY_SERVER_SIDE_GEMINI_API\"]\n}\n\n```\n\n--- /src/App.tsx ---\n```typescript\n/**\n * @license\n * SPDX-License-Identifier: Apache-2.0\n */\n\nexport default function App() {\n  return <div></div>;\n}\n\n```\n\n--- /src/index.css ---\n```css\n@import \"tailwindcss\";\n\n```\n\n--- /src/main.tsx ---\n```typescript\nimport {StrictMode} from \'react\';\nimport {createRoot} from \'react-dom/client\';\nimport App from \'./App.tsx\';\nimport \'./index.css\';\n\ncreateRoot(document.getElementById(\'root\')!).render(\n  <StrictMode>\n    <App />\n  </StrictMode>,\n);\n\n```\n\n--- /tsconfig.json ---\n```json\n{\n  \"compilerOptions\": {\n    \"target\": \"ES2022\",\n    \"experimentalDecorators\": true,\n    \"useDefineForClassFields\": false,\n    \"module\": \"ESNext\",\n    \"types\": [\"vite/client\"],\n    \"lib\": [\n      \"ES2022\",\n      \"DOM\",\n      \"DOM.Iterable\"\n    ],\n    \"skipLibCheck\": true,\n    \"moduleResolution\": \"bundler\",\n    \"isolatedModules\": true,\n    \"moduleDetection\": \"force\",\n    \"allowJs\": true,\n    \"jsx\": \"react-jsx\",\n    \"paths\": {\n      \"@/*\": [\n        \"./*\"\n      ]\n    },\n    \"allowImportingTsExtensions\": true,\n    \"noEmit\": true\n  }\n}\n\n```\n\n--- /vite.config.ts ---\n```typescript\nimport tailwindcss from \'@tailwindcss/vite\';\nimport react from \'@vitejs/plugin-react\';\nimport path from \'path\';\nimport {defineConfig} from \'vite\';\n\nexport default defineConfig(() => {\n  return {\n    plugins: [react(), tailwindcss()],\n    resolve: {\n      alias: {\n        \'@\': path.resolve(__dirname, \'.\'),\n      },\n    },\n    server: {\n      // HMR is disabled in AI Studio via DISABLE_HMR env var.\n      // Do not modify\303\242\302\200\302\224file watching is disabled to prevent flickering during agent edits.\n      hmr: process.env.DISABLE_HMR !== \'true\',\n      // Disable file watching when DISABLE_HMR is true to save CPU during agent edits.\n      watch: process.env.DISABLE_HMR === \'true\' ? null : {},\n    },\n  };\n});\n\n```"
