  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Analyzing Image Structure**\n\nI\'m currently focusing on a single image, specifically `image-1790114036816.png`. My analysis centers on its structural components. The background is a photorealistic alpine mountain landscape reflecting in a pristine lake or icy surface, with hints of snow and droplets. At the very top center, there\'s a giant embossed 3D transparent glass element.\n\n\n**Designing Interface Elements**\n\nI\'m now deep-diving into the user interface design. I\'ve sketched a top header/mode switcher with \"Weiss\" and \"Bunt\" options. I\'m also planning a left floating dock with icons. In a left glass card, I\'ll feature user profile info and an organized folder list. There are also middle top cards: note statistics, calendar, and last opened files. I\'m focusing on \"Guten Tag, Sascha\" for the title.\n\n\n**Developing Application Layout**\n\nI\'m now iterating on the bottom row card designs and a floating pill bar. These will feature \"Wetter\" (weather), \"KI-Einblick\" (AI insights), \"Verzeichnis\" (directory), \"To-dos\" (to-dos), and \"News\". The pill bar will have quick actions like new note creation, calendar access, and search. Clicking to-dos or a task opens a detailed checklist or RRF simulator in a glass modal. I\'m also examining the \"Atlas Lens\" image for inspiration, specifically its panoramic mountain window layout, integrating calendar, diagnostics, health metrics, and quick access buttons for this application\'s design.\n\n\n**Refining Visual Themes**\n\nI\'ve made significant progress in refining the visual themes. Specifically, \"Weiss\" and \"Bunt\" are being iterated on based on the imagery. Both have a mountain lake backdrop, but \"Weiss\" is now frosted ice glass, with navy typography and diamond refractions, while \"Bunt\" is holographic neon glass with electric glows and glowing text. The user can switch seamlessly between them with a single click. The content focuses on the project\'s Obsidian Vault, now with fully interactive widgets.\n\n\n**Structuring Application Features**\n\nI\'m now thinking about how to modularize the application. I\'ll construct `/src/components/GlassBackground.tsx` for the dynamic mountain lake backdrop, which adjusts to \"weiss\" (snow daylight) and \"bunt\" (sunset twilight). The sidebar will be `/src/components/GlassSidebar.tsx`, with the profile card as `/src/components/GlassProfileCard.tsx`. I\'ll also build `/src/components/GlassMetricsCard.tsx`, `/src/components/GlassCalendarCard.tsx`, `/src/components/GlassRecentNotesCard.tsx`, and `/src/components/GlassTodoWidget.tsx`. This includes interactive task features. Furthermore, I will create components to enhance user date navigation, and I\'ll make the profile section toggleable between \"Sascha\" and \"Vault Engine\".\n\n\n"
    thinking_duration {
      seconds: 9
      nanos: 61472371
    }
    stop_reason: STOP_REASON_STOP_PATTERN
  }
}
