  checkpoint {
    checkpoint_index: 1
    session_summary: "This summary captures the current state of the \"Glass Dashboard\" project, which has been fully implemented according to the user\'s specifications.\n\n### 1. Outstanding User Requests\n*   **\"das ist fertig?\" (Is this finished?):** The user is verifying the completion status of the project.\n    *   *Status:* **IMPLEMENTATION COMPLETE.** The dashboard is fully functional, styled, and integrated. No further coding tasks are currently pending.\n\n### 2. User Knowledge\n*   **Preferences & Aesthetic:** The user requires a \"Glassmorphism\" UI with two distinct modes:\n    *   **\"Weiss\":** Pure Crystal Ice Glass (light, clean, high-contrast).\n    *   **\"Bunt\":** Vibrant Sunset & Neon Holographic (darker, saturated, neon accents).\n*   **Scope:** The application is a dashboard for an Obsidian/MCP/Hybrid Retrieval system.\n*   **Key Decisions:**\n    *   The user requested a 32-chapter master task list with markdown export.\n    *   The user requested an interactive RRF (Reciprocal Rank Fusion) simulator to visualize hybrid search results.\n    *   The user requested a graph view for visualizing the Obsidian vault structure.\n*   **Data/Context:** The system uses mock data for tasks (`tasksData.ts`) and notes (`notesData.ts`) to drive the UI components.\n\n### 3. Work Accomplished\n*   **Dashboard UI:** Built a responsive, modular dashboard with a sidebar, metrics cards, calendar, and bottom navigation bar.\n*   **Theme Engine:** Implemented a persistent theme switcher (Weiss vs. Bunt) using `localStorage`.\n*   **Modals:**\n    *   **Checklist Modal:** Full 32-chapter task management with search, filtering, and markdown export.\n    *   **Simulator Modal:** RRF logic simulator with adjustable parameters ($k$, BM25 weight, Vector weight).\n    *   **Note Modal:** Interactive viewer/editor for vault notes.\n    *   **Graph Modal:** Interactive node-link visualization of the vault structure.\n*   **Data Integration:** Created `notesData.ts` to support the note viewer and populated the dashboard with relevant context (e.g., retrieval pipeline, MCP setup, Model2Vec details).\n*   **Refinement:** Resolved TypeScript linting errors regarding `TaskItem` property access (e.g., `chapterNumber`, `filename`, `summary`, `codeSnippets`) to ensure type safety.\n\n### 4. Model Knowledge\n*   **Architecture:** The application is a React SPA. State is managed via `useState` and `localStorage` for persistence.\n*   **Component Pattern:** The UI is composed of highly modular \"Glass\" components. Modals are handled via boolean state in `App.tsx` and conditionally rendered.\n*   **Styling:** Relies on Tailwind CSS with custom utility classes (`glass-white`, `glass-bunt`, `glass-rainbow-edge`) to achieve the frosted glass effect.\n*   **Data Flow:** `App.tsx` acts as the central orchestrator, passing `themeMode` and callback handlers to child components.\n*   **Constraint:** The `GlassChecklistModal` and `GlassSimulatorModal` require specific data structures defined in `tasksData.ts`. Any changes to the task schema must be reflected in `GlassChecklistModal.tsx`.\n\n### 5. Files and Code\n*   **Edited/Created Files:**\n    *   `/src/App.tsx`: Main orchestrator; manages global state, themes, and modal visibility.\n    *   `/src/components/GlassChecklistModal.tsx`: Implements the 32-chapter task list with filtering and export.\n    *   `/src/components/GlassSimulatorModal.tsx`: Implements the RRF algorithm simulation.\n    *   `/src/components/GlassNoteModal.tsx`: Created to view/edit markdown notes.\n    *   `/src/components/GlassGraphModal.tsx`: Created to visualize the Obsidian graph.\n    *   `/src/data/notesData.ts`: Created to store sample vault notes.\n    *   `/src/components/GlassWeatherStatusCard.tsx`, `/src/components/GlassAiInsightCard.tsx`, `/src/components/GlassDirectoryCard.tsx`, `/src/components/GlassTodoWidget.tsx`, `/src/components/GlassNewsCard.tsx`, `/src/components/GlassBottomBar.tsx`: Individual dashboard tiles/bars.\n\n### 6. Current Work and Next Steps\n*   **Status:** The project is feature-complete based on the initial requirements.\n*   **Next Steps:** No further development is required unless the user identifies specific bugs or requests additional features. The system is ready for deployment/integration into the user\'s actual Obsidian workflow."
    included_step_index_start: 64
    included_step_index_end: 107
    conversation_log_uris: "file:///.aistudio/artifacts/brain/701ae614-bcb5-4c42-8b5b-26b99136c74a/.system_generated/logs/transcript.jsonl"
    user_requests: "Here is the full initial file tree for the application:\n/.env.example\n/.gitignore\n/index.html\n/metadata.json\n/package.json\n/public/assets/aistudio/.gitignore\n/src/App.tsx\n/src/index.css\n/src/main.tsx\n/tsconfig.json\n/vite.config.ts\n\nThe following dependencies are installed:\n@google/genai: ^2.4.0\n@tailwindcss/vite: ^4.3.3\n@vitejs/plugin-react: ^6.1.1\ndotenv: ^17.2.3\nexpress: ^4.21.2\nlucide-react: ^0.546.0\nmotion: ^12.23.24\nreact: ^19.0.1\nreact-dom: ^19.0.1\nvite: ^8.3.0\n\nThe following devDependencies are installed:\n@types/express: ^4.17.21\n@types/node: ^22.14.0\n@types/react: ^19.3.0\n@types/react-dom: ^19.3.0\nautoprefixer: ^10.4.21\nesbuild: ^0.25.0\ntailwindcss: ^4.3.3\ntsx: ^4.21.0\ntypescript: ^7.0.2\n\nKey file contents:\n\n--- /.env.example ---\n```\n# GEMINI_API_KEY: Required for Gemini AI API calls.\n# AI Studio automatically injects this at runtime from user secrets.\n# Users configure this via the Secrets panel in the AI Studio UI.\nGEMINI_API_KEY=\"MY_GEMINI_API_KEY\"\n\n# APP_URL: The URL where this applet is hosted.\n# AI Studio automatically injects this at runtime with the Cloud Run service URL.\n# Used for self-referential links, OAuth callbacks, and API endpoints.\nAPP_URL=\"MY_APP_URL\"\n\n```\n\n--- /index.html ---\n```html\n<!doctype html>\n<html lang=\"en\">\n  <head>\n    <meta charset=\"UTF-8\" />\n    <meta name=\"viewport\" content=\"width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0\" />\n    <title>My Google AI Studio App</title>\n    <meta name=\"description\" content=\"An application built with Google AI Studio.\" />\n    <meta property=\"og:title\" content=\"My Google AI Studio App\" />\n    <meta property=\"og:description\" content=\"An application built with Google AI Studio.\" />\n    <meta property=\"og:type\" content=\"website\" />\n    <meta name=\"twitter:card\" content=\"summary_large_image\" />\n  </head>\n  <body>\n    <div id=\"root\"></div>\n    <script type=\"module\" src=\"/src/main.tsx\"></script>\n  </body>\n</html>\n\n\n```\n\n--- /metadata.json ---\n```json\n{\n  \"name\": \"\",\n  \"description\": \"\",\n  \"requestFramePermissions\": [],\n  \"majorCapabilities\": [\"MAJOR_CAPABILITY_SERVER_SIDE_GEMINI_API\"]\n}\n\n```\n\n--- /src/App.tsx ---\n```typescript\n/**\n * @license\n * SPDX-License-Identifier: Apache-2.0\n */\n\nexport default function App() {\n  return <div></div>;\n}\n\n```\n\n--- /src/index.css ---\n```css\n@import \"tailwindcss\";\n\n```\n\n--- /src/main.tsx ---\n```typescript\nimport {StrictMode} from \'react\';\nimport {createRoot} from \'react-dom/client\';\nimport App from \'./App.tsx\';\nimport \'./index.css\';\n\ncreateRoot(document.getElementById(\'root\')!).render(\n  <StrictMode>\n    <App />\n  </StrictMode>,\n);\n\n```\n\n--- /tsconfig.json ---\n```json\n{\n  \"compilerOptions\": {\n    \"target\": \"ES2022\",\n    \"experimentalDecorators\": true,\n    \"useDefineForClassFields\": false,\n    \"module\": \"ESNext\",\n    \"types\": [\"vite/client\"],\n    \"lib\": [\n      \"ES2022\",\n      \"DOM\",\n      \"DOM.Iterable\"\n    ],\n    \"skipLibCheck\": true,\n    \"moduleResolution\": \"bundler\",\n    \"isolatedModules\": true,\n    \"moduleDetection\": \"force\",\n    \"allowJs\": true,\n    \"jsx\": \"react-jsx\",\n    \"paths\": {\n      \"@/*\": [\n        \"./*\"\n      ]\n    },\n    \"allowImportingTsExtensions\": true,\n    \"noEmit\": true\n  }\n}\n\n```\n\n--- /vite.config.ts ---\n```typescript\nimport tailwindcss from \'@tailwindcss/vite\';\nimport react from \'@vitejs/plugin-react\';\nimport path from \'path\';\nimport {defineConfig} from \'vite\';\n\nexport default defineConfig(() => {\n  return {\n    plugins: [react(), tailwindcss()],\n    resolve: {\n      alias: {\n        \'@\': path.resolve(__dirname, \'.\'),\n      },\n    },\n    server: {\n      // HMR is disabled in AI Studio via DISABLE_HMR env var.\n      // Do not modify\303\242\302\200\302\224file watching is disabled to prevent flickering during agent edits.\n      hmr: process.env.DISABLE_HMR !== \'true\',\n      // Disable file watching when DISABLE_HMR is true to save CPU during agent edits.\n      watch: process.env.DISABLE_HMR === \'true\' ? null : {},\n    },\n  };\n});\n\n```"
