  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Analyzing Component Structure**\n\nI\'m currently focused on `GlassAudioPlayerModal.tsx`, specifically lines 24-46. The goal is to understand how the component handles its visibility and theme-specific rendering based on `isOpen` and `themeMode`. It seems like the component renders conditionally based on the `isOpen` prop, returning `null` if not open.\n\n\n**Refactoring Player States**\n\nI\'m now restructuring the component to initialize all state variables and references at the top. This includes `useState` and `useRef` hooks for managing playback state, voice selection, and progress. I\'m also considering the conditional rendering based on `isOpen`, and I\'ll ensure playback is stopped when the modal is closed and returning `null`. I\'m starting by examining the `useEffect` hook to see how it initializes available voices.\n\n\n**Examining Voice Initialization**\n\nI\'m now diving into the voice initialization logic within the `useEffect` hook. I\'m focusing on how the component filters available voices to German ones, prioritizes Google or Natural voices if available, and sets the `selectedVoice`. I see the `updateVoices` function retrieves voices on component mount and updates when voices change, also canceling speech on unmount. I\'m also ensuring the speech is stopped when the modal is closed.\n\n\n"
    tool_calls {
      id: "call_1478576"
      name: "edit_file"
      arguments_json: "{\"Instruction\":\"Move hooks before early return and handle cleanup on close in GlassAudioPlayerModal\", \"ReplacementContent\":\"export const GlassAudioPlayerModal = ({ isOpen, onClose, themeMode }: Props) => {\\n  const isWeiss = themeMode === \'weiss\';\\n  const [currentChapterIdx, setCurrentChapterIdx] = useState(0);\\n  const [isPlaying, setIsPlaying] = useState(false);\\n  const [rate, setRate] = useState(1.0);\\n  const [selectedVoice, setSelectedVoice] = useState<SpeechSynthesisVoice | null>(null);\\n  const [availableVoices, setAvailableVoices] = useState<SpeechSynthesisVoice[]>([]);\\n  const [progressPercent, setProgressPercent] = useState(0);\\n  const [isMuted, setIsMuted] = useState(false);\\n\\n  const utteranceRef = useRef<SpeechSynthesisUtterance | null>(null);\\n  const progressTimerRef = useRef<any>(null);\\n\\n  const currentChapter = AUDIO_EXPLANATION_CHAPTERS[currentChapterIdx] || AUDIO_EXPLANATION_CHAPTERS[0];\\n\\n  // Initialize available German voices\\n  useEffect(() => {\\n    const updateVoices = () => {\\n      if (typeof window !== \'undefined\' && \'speechSynthesis\' in window) {\\n        const voices = window.speechSynthesis.getVoices();\\n        const germanVoices = voices.filter(\\n          (v) => v.lang.startsWith(\'de\') || v.lang.startsWith(\'DE\')\\n        );\\n        setAvailableVoices(germanVoices.length > 0 ? germanVoices : voices);\\n\\n        // Pick best natural German voice\\n        const preferred =\\n          germanVoices.find((v) => v.name.includes(\'Google\') || v.name.includes(\'Natural\')) ||\\n          germanVoices[0] ||\\n          voices[0];\\n        if (preferred) setSelectedVoice(preferred);\\n      }\\n    };\\n\\n    updateVoices();\\n    if (typeof window !== \'undefined\' && \'speechSynthesis\' in window) {\\n      window.speechSynthesis.onvoiceschanged = updateVoices;\\n    }\\n\\n    return () => {\\n      if (typeof window !== \'undefined\' && \'speechSynthesis\' in window) {\\n        window.speechSynthesis.cancel();\\n      }\\n    };\\n  }, []);\\n\\n  // Cleanup playback if modal closes\\n  useEffect(() => {\\n    if (!isOpen) {\\n      if (typeof window !== \'undefined\' && \'speechSynthesis\' in window) {\\n        window.speechSynthesis.cancel();\\n      }\\n      clearInterval(progressTimerRef.current);\\n      setIsPlaying(false);\\n    }\\n  }, [isOpen]);\\n\\n  if (!isOpen) return null;\", \"TargetContent\":\"export const GlassAudioPlayerModal = ({ isOpen, onClose, themeMode }: Props) => {\\n  if (!isOpen) return null;\\n\\n  const isWeiss = themeMode === \'weiss\';\\n  const [currentChapterIdx, setCurrentChapterIdx] = useState(0);\\n  const [isPlaying, setIsPlaying] = useState(false);\\n  const [rate, setRate] = useState(1.0);\\n  const [selectedVoice, setSelectedVoice] = useState<SpeechSynthesisVoice | null>(null);\\n  const [availableVoices, setAvailableVoices] = useState<SpeechSynthesisVoice[]>([]);\\n  const [progressPercent, setProgressPercent] = useState(0);\\n  const [isMuted, setIsMuted] = useState(false);\\n\\n  const utteranceRef = useRef<SpeechSynthesisUtterance | null>(null);\\n  const progressTimerRef = useRef<any>(null);\\n\\n  const currentChapter = AUDIO_EXPLANATION_CHAPTERS[currentChapterIdx];\\n\\n  // Initialize available German voices\\n  useEffect(() => {\\n    const updateVoices = () => {\\n      if (typeof window !== \'undefined\' && \'speechSynthesis\' in window) {\\n        const voices = window.speechSynthesis.getVoices();\\n        const germanVoices = voices.filter(\\n          (v) => v.lang.startsWith(\'de\') || v.lang.startsWith(\'DE\')\\n        );\\n        setAvailableVoices(germanVoices.length > 0 ? germanVoices : voices);\\n\\n        // Pick best natural German voice\\n        const preferred =\\n          germanVoices.find((v) => v.name.includes(\'Google\') || v.name.includes(\'Natural\')) ||\\n          germanVoices[0] ||\\n          voices[0];\\n        if (preferred) setSelectedVoice(preferred);\\n      }\\n    };\\n\\n    updateVoices();\\n    if (typeof window !== \'undefined\' && \'speechSynthesis\' in window) {\\n      window.speechSynthesis.onvoiceschanged = updateVoices;\\n    }\\n\\n    return () => {\\n      if (typeof window !== \'undefined\' && \'speechSynthesis\' in window) {\\n        window.speechSynthesis.cancel();\\n      }\\n    };\\n  }, []);\", \"TargetFile\":\"/src/components/GlassAudioPlayerModal.tsx\", \"toolAction\":\"Fixing hook order in GlassAudioPlayerModal\", \"toolSummary\":\"Move hooks before early return in GlassAudioPlayerModal\"}"
